block a regressed handler would produce:
"telegram.info_requested_by_label: \ntelegram.info_url_label: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2212"

the URL it shows is "https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2212",
built as REPO_URL + "/issues/2212" — so it contains REPO_URL by construction,
which is why a containment check could not tell this block from a correct one.

new  urlLineOf(block).url === REPO_URL  on the regressed block -> false  (fails — the bug is caught)
new  urlLineOf(block).url === REPO_URL  on the correct block   -> true  (passes)

✅ the tightened assertion catches a mislabelling containment could not
✅ the tightened assertion still passes on the correct block
